abstract: >-
  Oracle3 is an open-source trading engine and Model Context Protocol server
  for prediction markets. It maps logical relations between event contracts,
  checks whether quoted prices violate the axioms of probability after each
  venue's published fees, and trades the baskets that survive, live on Kalshi,
  Polymarket and Solana or on paper, under pre-trade risk limits. It includes six
  constraint-based, two statistical-arbitrage and two model-driven strategies,
  and a fair-value engine based on the Wang transform calibrated on 291,309
  resolved contracts.
